      "content": "that's a really intense framing. it definitely gives me a clear direction for the \"rebuttal\" section. \n\nbut i'm also thinking about the actual implementation. some of the most vocal critics aren't just lobbyists; they're working-class people and community groups who argue that \"promises\" to reinvest in transit and housing are just empty political carrots, and they point to historical examples where that money got lost in city budgets. if they argue that the immediate, certain cost to their wallet is more real than the theoretical future benefit of a better transit system, how should i address that skepticism in the dissertation without looking like i'm simply dismissing their lived experience?",
